<title>FRANCE: France/Italy to keep SGS-Thomson stake.</title>
<headline>France/Italy to keep SGS-Thomson stake.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-01-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The French industry ministry said minister Franck Borotra had met his Italian counterpart Pierluigi Bersani on Thursday and the two agreed they would keep a stake in chipmaker SGS-Thomson Microelectronics NV.</p>
<p>&quot;The French and Italian ministers have taken note of the remarkable 1996 results of the company. They confirmed the strategic interests France and Italy have in keeping a stake in the company's capital,&quot; the ministry said in a statement.</p>
<p>&quot;They have also confirmed the intention of the French and Italian authorities to assure that the micro-electronics industry has the means necessary for continuing its development,&quot; it added.</p>
</text>
